# Vercel Speed Insights Installation Report

## Summary
Successfully installed and configured Vercel Speed Insights for the Shakti Alloys website (Vite + React + TypeScript project).

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- Installed `@vercel/speed-insights@^2.0.0` package using npm
- Package added to dependencies in `package.json`
- Lock file (`package-lock.json`) updated with new dependency tree

### 2. Code Integration
Modified `src/main.tsx`:
- Added import: `import { SpeedInsights } from '@vercel/speed-insights/react'`
- Added `<SpeedInsights />` component to the React render tree, positioned after the existing `<Analytics />` component
- Follows the same pattern as the existing Vercel Analytics integration

### 3. Implementation Details
- Used the React-specific package path (`@vercel/speed-insights/react`) as per official Vercel documentation for Vite/React projects
- Placed the component at the root level in `main.tsx` to ensure it tracks all page interactions
- Positioned alongside the existing `@vercel/analytics` component for consistency

### 4. Verification
- TypeScript type checking: ✅ Passed
- Production build: ✅ Successfully built
- No errors or warnings introduced

## Files Modified
1. `package.json` - Added @vercel/speed-insights dependency
2. `package-lock.json` - Updated with new dependency tree
3. `src/main.tsx` - Added SpeedInsights component import and usage

## Framework-Specific Notes
This is a Vite + React + TypeScript project, so I followed the official Vercel documentation for React/Vite projects:
- Package used: `@vercel/speed-insights/react`
- Component: `<SpeedInsights />`
- Location: Root-level in main.tsx for comprehensive tracking

## Next Steps
Once deployed to Vercel, Speed Insights will automatically begin collecting Core Web Vitals and performance metrics. The tracking script will be served from `/_vercel/speed-insights/*` routes.

No additional configuration is required. The Speed Insights dashboard will be available in the Vercel project dashboard after deployment.
